This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-kiss layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

  Internal dependency on meta-kiss.

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  branch: scarthgap

  URI: git://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-arm
  branch: scarthgap

Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-kiss layer as patches to
feedback@bootlin.com or as github pull requests at
https://github.com/bootlin/yocto-kiss

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-kiss-nxp layer to your build
 II. Misc


I. Adding the meta-kiss-nxp layer to your build
======================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-kiss-nxp'

II. Misc
========

This layer extend the simple meta-kiss layer with more complex
architectures that need specific firmwares with more nested boot flow.
It is not useful as is, but rather as a reference on how a layer can
be written without unnecessary complications.

freiheit93 feature status (2026-07-13)
=======================================

Boots end-to-end (SPL/ATF/U-Boot/kernel/rootfs) to a login prompt.
Hardware-verified feature status beyond the base boot:

  WiFi          - working. On-board combo chip is the NXP IW612
                  (SDIO vendor 0x0471/device 0x0205, btnxpuart ChipID
                  0x7601 - not the Marvell 88W8987 the upstream DTS
                  bluetooth node's compatible string suggests).
                  Mainline mwifiex has no IW612 ID table entry, so
                  this uses NXP's downstream kernel-module-nxp-wlan
                  (moal/mlan), patched to build against the real
                  (non-wireless_dev) mainline cfg80211 API.

  Bluetooth     - firmware present and requested correctly by the
                  in-tree btnxpuart driver (same firmware package as
                  WiFi, firmware-nxp-wifi-nxpiw612-sdio), but bringing
                  hci0 up reproducibly fails with
                  "Opcode 0x0c03 failed: -110" (HCI Reset timeout).
                  The lpuart5 DTS node has uart-has-rtscts and a
                  dedicated reset-gpios line, and its vcc-supply is
                  the SAME regulator as the WiFi SDIO function
                  (reg_usdhc3_vmmc) - possible power/reset sequencing
                  interaction between the two radios of the combo
                  chip. Not yet root-caused.

  M33/rpmsg     - imx-m33-demos firmware deploys correctly to
                  /lib/firmware. remoteproc0 comes up "attached"
                  (TF-A already started the M33 core before Linux
                  boots), but `echo stop > .../state` fails ("Not in
                  wfi, force stopped" / "Failed to stop remote core").
                  Loading a new demo image via pure Linux remoteproc
                  therefore doesn't currently work from the attached
                  state. Likely needs the U-Boot bootaux path instead
                  (would require IMAGE_BOOT_FILES/WKS_FILE_DEPENDS
                  wiring that was deliberately left out when this was
                  first added, on the assumption the attached-state
                  stop/start cycle would just work).

  MIPI-DSI/CSI  - kernel-side prep only (CONFIG_DRM_IMX93_MIPI_DSI).
                  No display or camera hardware attached to verify
                  against. Mainline's imx91_93_common.dtsi has no
                  lcdif/dsi/ldb DT nodes yet (NXP downstream carries
                  them) - a future panel bring-up needs those nodes
                  added, not just kernel config. i.MX93 also has no
                  mainline driver for its DWC MIPI CSI-2 host, so
                  camera capture isn't possible with mainline alone
                  yet regardless of sensor choice.

  MQS audio     - working. mqs-audio ALSA card present,
                  speaker-test/aplay produce real 48kHz stereo PCM
                  output (alsa-utils-aplay/-speaker-test pulled in
                  via CORE_IMAGE_EXTRA_INSTALL in the kas config, not
                  this layer).
